p.src:
Solving Eq.  for the angular velocity gives $\dot\theta=\frac{L}{mr^2}.$ Substitution into Eq.  yields $\begin{aligned}
 m\ddot r
 &=-\frac{dU}{dr}
   +mr\left(\frac{L}{mr^2}\right)^2 \\
 &=-\frac{dU}{dr}+\frac{L^2}{mr^3}.
 \end{aligned}$

